# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY TRACKED, so that a later edit has to argue with a
# sentence before it can drop it:
#
#   results/*.json   THE EVIDENCE. Every number in README.md is derived from
#                    these by scripts/check_readme_numbers.py, and the test
#                    suite asserts against them. A repository that ignored
#                    them would pass every existence check and be useless.
#   sql/, scripts/   the schema, the generator and the experiments
#   stack/           the compose file
#
# data/ IS DELIBERATELY NOT TRACKED, AND THAT IS NOT THE SAME DECISION AS
# ignoring the evidence. The CSVs are a pure function of the seed: scripts/
# generate_roster.py rebuilds them byte for byte, and every results file
# carries the manifest sha256 of the input it was measured on, so a reader who
# regenerates can prove they hold the same rows rather than take it on trust.
# Committing 75,000 generated rows would add megabytes that say nothing the
# hash does not already say.
#
# Excluded below is only what a clone can rebuild.

data
envs
.venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
*.pyc
.DS_Store
